 "remarks": "Imagine ending every day with the sky turning shades of pink, violet and gold over the Long Island Sound, right from your own deck. This classic shingle-style beach house at 25 Compo Beach Road offers a front-row seat to the very best of Westport's coastal lifestyle. Positioned with direct waterfront views of Gray's Creek, the home captures the true essence of shorefront living, where the rhythm of the tides and the salt air become part of your daily routine.  The architecture honors the timeless tradition of New England beach homes, blending weathered shingles with an interior designed to maximize the stunning vistas. Windows invite the light in, framing the sparkling water and the masts of boats at the nearby Ned Dimes Marina. Whether you're hosting an al fresco dinner or enjoying a quiet morning with coffee overlooking the creek, the connection to the water is seamless.  Location is everything here. You are just steps from the sandy shores of Compo Beach and Ned Dimes Marina, making it effortless to enjoy the waterfront amenities and the vibrant maritime atmosphere that defines this coveted stretch of the Connecticut coastline. It's more than just a house; it's a retreat where the sunset views are spectacular and the coastal charm is unmatched.",
